{"type":"text","timestamp":1790375660562,"sessionID":"ses_f254c5965ffe7kqk7x65zPgWlx","part":{"id":"prt_0dab48bf1001i4lgEgmtQZAHYV","messageID":"msg_0dab43ccf001LaMZ4KIlPqJCQc","sessionID":"ses_f254c5965ffe7kqk7x65zPgWlx","type":"text","text":"The main scene already assigns ships to `fleet_a` and `fleet_b`. I’ll use a base range of 32 pixels, so the player’s attack range of 2 detects the enemy at 60 pixels while leaving the one at 125 pixels outside. The signal connections also need to account for `TargetFinder` becoming ready before the battle unit’s `@onready` variables initialize.\n","time":{"start":1790375660529,"end":1790375660534},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0fbdbffde444c1e1016ab6f6e7f7b487d2b338e175e32b1110","phase":"commentary"}}}}
